@ERRORS ON and OFF
.
=ERRORS ON AND OFF
.
.ERRORS OFF leaves out the run-time index checks on arrays in the code after
.it. ERRORS ON puts them back. ON is the default.
.
:DIM B(10) AS UBYTE, I AS UBYTE
:ERRORS OFF
:B(I) = 1
:ERRORS ON
.
.  - The switch follows the source, not the run: it applies to the lines
.    below it in the file.
.  - With the checks off, an index out of range reads or writes the memory
.    past the array.
.  - Code under ERRORS OFF is smaller and faster.
.  - A constant index is checked at compile time in both modes.
.
.See Arrays.
.
=SEE ALSO
.
>16|Arrays
